WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:06.540
A talking hippo, a mystic bangle, and psychic&nbsp;
communication with a dinosaur? All in Marvel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:11.700
shows? In order for all this insanity to make&nbsp;
sense you'll have to watch them in this order!

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:16.140
Warning: This video contains fast, flashing&nbsp;
images. Viewer discretion is advised,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:18.468
especially for those with photosensitive epilepsy.

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:23.820
"Agent Carter" — which aired two seasons&nbsp;
on ABC from 2015 to 2016 — is our starting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:27.180
point, as it's the best overall&nbsp;
introduction to the Marvel world.

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:32.040
It's also the earliest program in Marvel's&nbsp;
in-story chronology. The events of "Agent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:36.900
Carter" occur following 2011's "Captain America:&nbsp;
The First Avenger," with Hayley Atwell reprising&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:41.100
her role as Peggy Carter. Rather than revolve&nbsp;
solely around the eponymous protagonist,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:45.900
"Agent Carter" delves deeper into the backstory&nbsp;
of characters like Edwin Jarvis, Howard Stark,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:50.340
Daniel Sousa, and Dottie Underwood who&nbsp;
all have wider connections to the MCU.

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:54.660
Unfortunately, ABC canceled "Agent Carter" before&nbsp;
it could fully depict the origins of S.H.I.E.L.D.,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:58.920
as it was originally billed to do.&nbsp;
The second season ends in 1946,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:03.060
while Peggy doesn't become the director&nbsp;
of S.H.I.E.L.D. until 1949. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:08.460
while the series doesn't quite fulfill its initial&nbsp;
directive, it's still a solid, entertaining show&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:12.480
that helps to establish a stronger backstory&nbsp;
for Peggy, so it shouldn't be missed.

00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:17.668
"Strategic homeland intervention&nbsp;
enforcement and logistics division.”

00:01:17.668 --> 00:01:18.840
“And what does that mean to you?”

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:21.480
“It means someone really wanted&nbsp;
our initials to spell out SHIELD."

00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:26.940
In 2013, Marvel Television launched "Agents&nbsp;
of S.H.I.E.L.D." on ABC. The series introduces&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.940 --> 00:01:31.860
viewers to a group of S.H.I.E.L.D. agents led by&nbsp;
the recently revived Phil Coulson, played by Clark&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:36.780
Gregg, who is seemingly killed by Loki, played&nbsp;
by Tom Hiddleston, in 2012's "The Avengers."

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:40.860
"S.H.I.E.L.D." begins after the events&nbsp;
of "The Avengers" and 2013's "Iron Man&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:43.920
3." Although it more or less&nbsp;
evolves into a standalone show,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:49.260
Seasons 1 and 2 of "S.H.I.E.L.D." closely follow&nbsp;
events from the MCU film timeline. For example,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.260 --> 00:01:54.840
in Season 1, Episode 8 follows up on the aftermath&nbsp;
of 2013's "Thor: The Dark World," and the Season&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:59.340
1 finale mirrors the events that take place in&nbsp;
2014's "Captain America: The Winter Soldier."

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:03.660
The series also includes brief appearances&nbsp;
from Nick Fury, played by Samuel L. Jackson,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.660 --> 00:02:08.460
and Maria Hill, played by Cobie Smulders.&nbsp;
When S.H.I.E.L.D. is destroyed, Fury puts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:13.680
Coulson in charge of rebuilding the agency his&nbsp;
own way from the ground up. This rebuilding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:18.660
proves both figurative and literal, in the&nbsp;
respect that it marks a point for "Agents&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:22.935
of S.H.I.E.L.D." to go in a new direction,&nbsp;
away from rigidly following the MCU timeline.

00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:27.600
Netflix's Marvel era started in 2015&nbsp;
with "Daredevil" and "Jessica Jones."

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:32.820
"Daredevil" — which stars Charlie Cox as&nbsp;
Daredevil, aka Matt Murdock — arrived on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:38.340
the streamer first. As a blind lawyer by day and&nbsp;
a vigilante by night, Murdock does everything he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:42.060
can to protect the residents of the section&nbsp;
of New York City known as Hell's Kitchen.

00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:46.500
"Daredevil" makes sense to watch after the first&nbsp;
two seasons of "S.H.I.E.L.D." for a couple of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:51.180
reasons. First, the first episode of "Daredevil"&nbsp;
explains that something like a couple of years&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.180 --> 00:02:55.680
has passed since the Battle of New York from&nbsp;
"The Avengers," which means "Daredevil" begins&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.680 --> 00:03:01.320
around the time Season 2 of "S.H.I.E.L.D." ends.&nbsp;
Second, Episode 2 references Carl "Crusher" Creel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:05.220
aka Absorbing Man, a villain who&nbsp;
shows up in Season 2 of "S.H.I.E.L.D."

00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:09.780
"Daredevil" is also the perfect foundation for&nbsp;
introducing the rest of New York's street-level&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.780 --> 00:03:14.760
vigilantes, making it the obvious segue&nbsp;
into "Jessica Jones." Krysten Ritter plays&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:19.740
the reluctant do-gooder who's sworn off superhero&nbsp;
life, opting to put her powers to use as a private&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.740 --> 00:03:24.360
investigator. The first season follows Jessica&nbsp;
Jones as she deals with a demon from her past.

00:03:24.900 --> 00:03:29.280
For an intuitive watching sequence,&nbsp;
"Daredevil" Season 2 is the thematic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:32.940
choice after "Jessica Jones" Season&nbsp;
1, and "Luke Cage" comes after.

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:36.960
Season 1 of "Jessica Jones" introduces&nbsp;
Luke Cage, played by Mike Colter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:41.880
so you'll already be familiar with Netflix's third&nbsp;
vigilante hero if you follow our watch order.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.880 --> 00:03:45.780
The first season of "Luke Cage" overlaps&nbsp;
with "Daredevil" Season 2 a little bit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:48.960
so we recommend watching them one&nbsp;
after the other. By the end of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:52.918
first season of "Luke Cage," the events&nbsp;
of "Daredevil" Season 2 have taken place.

00:03:52.918 --> 00:03:59.304
"The more I hit him, the more he dished&nbsp;
out. So I stopped feeding him hate."

00:03:59.340 --> 00:04:05.040
Danny Rand, played by Finn Jones, rounds out&nbsp;
Netflix's roster of righteous vigilantes. Rand,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:09.780
aka Iron Fist, gets his mystical powers by&nbsp;
defeating the dragon Shou-Lao, rather than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.780 --> 00:04:14.520
from accidental or external forces, as is more&nbsp;
typically the case for New York's street-level&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:19.140
heroes. Debuting on Netflix in 2017, the&nbsp;
series follows Danny Rand as he returns&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.140 --> 00:04:23.340
to New York with his powers. When the pressure&nbsp;
of being the last living member of the wealthy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.340 --> 00:04:27.840
Rand Family combines with the duties of the&nbsp;
Iron Fist, it turns out to be a lot to handle.

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:32.640
After watching the first season of "Iron Fist,"&nbsp;
you'll be primed for "The Defenders" — a limited&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.640 --> 00:04:37.500
series that brings together the title characters&nbsp;
from four of Netflix's Marvel shows. It takes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:42.840
place several weeks after the events of Season 1&nbsp;
of "Iron Fist," but picks up story threads from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:47.760
all four associated programs. Showrunner Marco&nbsp;
Ramirez explained in a Den of Geek article,

00:05:03.668 --> 00:05:10.320
"Daredevil" introduces Jon Bernthal's take on&nbsp;
Frank Castle, aka the Punisher — a quintessential&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.320 --> 00:05:15.660
antihero whose methods of cleaning up New York&nbsp;
City tend to get a little more homicidal than his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:20.760
fellow crimefighters. Before his own show starts,&nbsp;
he's last seen in the "Daredevil" Season 2 finale,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.760 --> 00:05:24.900
but doesn't reprise his role for "The&nbsp;
Defenders." "The Punisher" provides an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.900 --> 00:05:29.220
in-story explanation for Frank's absence from&nbsp;
the limited series, although showrunner Marco&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:33.240
Ramirez told The Hollywood Reporter the real&nbsp;
culprit was Bernthal's lack of availability.

00:05:33.240 --> 00:05:36.360
When "The Punisher" begins, a few&nbsp;
months on from the most recent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.360 --> 00:05:39.900
events of "Daredevil," Frank Castle is&nbsp;
working in construction under the name&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:43.200
Pete Castiglione. He doesn't&nbsp;
remain in retirement for long.

00:05:43.200 --> 00:05:46.620
Netflix canceled "The Punisher"&nbsp;
after two seasons — which we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.620 --> 00:05:49.920
recommend watching back-to-back&nbsp;
after "The Defenders." In 2020,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.920 --> 00:05:54.060
writer-director Adam G. Simon pitched a film&nbsp;
based on "The Punisher" to Marvel Studios.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.060 --> 00:05:59.220
He imagined it would be tonally similar to a&nbsp;
film like "Logan" per Comicbook.com. He added,

00:06:14.734 --> 00:06:18.540
Sadly, it's unlikely Simon's pitch&nbsp;
will ever come to fruition ... but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.540 --> 00:06:21.900
that doesn't mean we'll never see&nbsp;
Frank Castle again in the MCU.

00:06:22.134 --> 00:06:27.960
Since Jessica Jones, Luke Cage, and Danny Rand are&nbsp;
fresh from their foray together as the Defenders,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.960 --> 00:06:31.380
it makes sense to continue their stories&nbsp;
before moving back to "S.H.I.E.L.D."

00:06:31.380 --> 00:06:35.640
Out of these three second seasons, it makes&nbsp;
the most sense to start with "Jessica Jones,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.640 --> 00:06:40.080
chronologically. There's a lot going on in&nbsp;
"Jessica Jones'' Season 2; the reluctant hero&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:44.280
struggles to move past her recent encounters with&nbsp;
Kilgrave, played by David Tennant. In addition,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.280 --> 00:06:48.900
the sophomore batch of "Jessica Jones'' episodes&nbsp;
bring a lot more of her history to the screen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.900 --> 00:06:51.960
including the story behind how&nbsp;
exactly she got her powers.

00:06:51.960 --> 00:06:56.460
Season 2 of "Luke Cage" — in which the&nbsp;
man with unbreakable skin has become a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.460 --> 00:07:00.780
sort of superhero mascot of Harlem, and must&nbsp;
contend with the baggage and responsibilities&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.780 --> 00:07:05.460
of celebrity – is the natural progression&nbsp;
from Season 2 of "Jessica Jones." Danny&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.460 --> 00:07:09.240
Rand appears in Season 2 of "Luke Cage"&nbsp;
before the second season of "Iron Fist,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:13.260
and it's more than a mere cameo. After&nbsp;
the crossover, there are three episodes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.260 --> 00:07:17.595
of "Luke Cage" left to watch before you&nbsp;
can dive into Season 2 of "Iron Fist."

00:07:17.640 --> 00:07:25.314
"But this city rejected you,&nbsp;
it beat you. I beat you."

00:07:25.314 --> 00:07:31.260
Out of Marvel's Netflix shows, only "Daredevil"&nbsp;
and "Jessica Jones" return for a third season, so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.260 --> 00:07:35.400
it makes the most sense to watch them when their&nbsp;
previous seasons are still fresh in your mind.

00:07:35.400 --> 00:07:38.880
Daredevil is last seen several&nbsp;
in-story months ago in "The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.880 --> 00:07:43.080
Defenders." Viewers know he survives&nbsp;
after seemingly sacrificing himself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.080 --> 00:07:48.300
and this third season clarifies exactly how&nbsp;
that happens. Meanwhile, the third season of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:52.620
"Jessica Jones" picks up about three months&nbsp;
after the events of Season 2. Viewers who are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.620 --> 00:07:57.780
correctly miffed that "Luke Cage" comes to&nbsp;
an abrupt and inconclusive end with Season 2&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.780 --> 00:08:03.360
can enjoy some degree of closure when he briefly&nbsp;
returns in the series finale of "Jessica Jones."

00:08:03.360 --> 00:08:07.500
Both "Daredevil" and "Jessica Jones''&nbsp;
conclude with their third seasons,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.500 --> 00:08:12.360
temporarily bringing the storylines of all&nbsp;
of Netflix's vigilantes to a close. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.360 --> 00:08:18.045
whether they're all gone for good remains&nbsp;
to be seen. In 2021, audiences saw Daredevil&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.045 --> 00:08:22.500
reemerge in "Spider-Man: No Way Home," and&nbsp;
The Kingpin, played by Vincent D'Onofrio,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.500 --> 00:08:28.829
return to television in Disney+'s "Hawkeye."&nbsp;
Could more Jessica Jones or Luke Cage be far off?

00:08:28.860 --> 00:08:34.320
After watching every season of Marvel's&nbsp;
streaming Netflix shows uninterrupted — which,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.320 --> 00:08:37.500
let's be honest, just makes sense —&nbsp;
it's time to check in with Director&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.500 --> 00:08:39.720
Phil Coulson and his team from network television.

00:08:39.720 --> 00:08:44.280
While the third season of "S.H.I.E.L.D." was&nbsp;
broadcast around the same time as 2015's "Ant-Man&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.280 --> 00:08:49.320
'' and 2016's "Captain America: Civil War '' hit&nbsp;
theaters, the show stopped reflecting the events&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.320 --> 00:08:54.720
of the MCU after Season 2, forging ahead in its&nbsp;
own direction. The second season ends with a box&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:54.720 --> 00:09:00.180
of Terrigen crystals falling into the ocean and&nbsp;
contaminating Earth's water supply, causing anyone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.180 --> 00:09:04.800
with Inhuman DNA to go through the Terrigenesis&nbsp;
process that activates their innate powers.

00:09:04.800 --> 00:09:09.960
While some S.H.I.E.L.D. agents search for&nbsp;
Inhumans, Daisy Johnson, played by Chloe Bennet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:09.960 --> 00:09:14.880
gets a handle on her Inhuman powers and&nbsp;
builds a team of Secret Warriors. Meanwhile,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.880 --> 00:09:19.080
Grant Ward, played by Brett Dalton,&nbsp;
looks to rebuild HYDRA, and Leo Fitz,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:19.080 --> 00:09:24.180
played by Iain De Caestecker, figures out that&nbsp;
the Monolith is an extraterrestrial portal that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:24.180 --> 00:09:28.500
may have transported Jemma Simmons, played by&nbsp;
Elizabeth Henstridge, to an unknown planet.

00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:33.734
If that makes it sound like "S.H.I.E.L.D." Season&nbsp;
3 has a lot to unpack, that's because it does.

00:09:33.960 --> 00:09:38.100
The third season of "Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D."&nbsp;
deals with alien planets, Terrigenesis,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:38.100 --> 00:09:42.120
and the search for more Inhumans. All&nbsp;
those Inhuman-related components make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.120 --> 00:09:46.080
"S.H.I.E.L.D" Season 3 the perfect&nbsp;
predecessor to Marvel's "Inhumans."

00:09:46.301 --> 00:09:53.081
"We face an uncertain future,&nbsp;
but we face it with hope."

00:09:53.081 --> 00:09:58.560
In 2017, the first two episodes of "Inhumans" were&nbsp;
released in IMAX theaters before the remaining six&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.560 --> 00:10:03.600
episodes premiered on ABC. This single-season&nbsp;
series follows the Inhuman Royal Family,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:03.600 --> 00:10:09.480
led by King Blackagar Boltagon, aka Black Bolt,&nbsp;
played by Anson Mount. Generations ago, Black&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:09.480 --> 00:10:15.000
Bolt fled Earth and created Attilan, an Inhuman&nbsp;
safe haven on the Moon. When Black Bolt notices&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:15.000 --> 00:10:20.220
the Terrigen outbreak on Earth, from Seasons 2 and&nbsp;
3 of "S.H.I.E.L.D.", he sends his cousin Triton,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:20.220 --> 00:10:25.500
played by Mike Moh, to rescue any Inhumans who&nbsp;
are on the run and bring them back to Attilan.

00:10:25.500 --> 00:10:29.940
However, this doesn't exactly go according to&nbsp;
plan when Black Bolt's mad brother Maximus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:29.940 --> 00:10:33.051
played by Iwan Rheon, tries to usurp the throne.

00:10:33.120 --> 00:10:37.800
"Inhumans" might not technically be an&nbsp;
"Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D." spinoff, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:37.800 --> 00:10:42.840
"Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D.: Slingshot" clearly is.&nbsp;
The six-part web series focuses on S.H.I.E.L.D.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:42.840 --> 00:10:47.880
newcomer Elena "Yo-Yo" Rodriguez, played by&nbsp;
Natalia Cordova-Buckley. Yo-Yo is being forced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:47.880 --> 00:10:52.380
to sign the Sokovia Accords, but this interferes&nbsp;
with a personal mission she must complete.

00:10:52.380 --> 00:10:56.520
"Slingshot" was technically released midway&nbsp;
through the fourth season of "S.H.I.E.L.D.",&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:56.520 --> 00:11:00.000
but the events in it take place before&nbsp;
the beginning of the season. The main&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:03.840
cast members of "S.H.I.E.L.D." are also&nbsp;
present in "Slingshot." Cordova-Buckley&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:03.840 --> 00:11:06.480
explained to IGN that the web&nbsp;
series is meant to help viewers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:06.480 --> 00:11:10.980
"understand the reasoning for many of the&nbsp;
decisions that characters make in Season 4."

00:11:10.980 --> 00:11:14.880
"Slingshot" also realigns "S.H.I.E.L.D."&nbsp;
with the MCU timeline, placing it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:14.880 --> 00:11:18.600
sometime after the Sokovia Accords are&nbsp;
introduced in 2016's "Captain America:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:18.600 --> 00:11:22.440
Civil War." The relationship between&nbsp;
"S.H.I.E.L.D." and the MCU timeline&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:22.440 --> 00:11:27.480
becomes even clearer with the introduction of&nbsp;
Robbie Reyes, played by Gabriel Luna — thus far,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:27.480 --> 00:11:32.640
the only version of Ghost Rider to canonically&nbsp;
appear in any MCU-adjacent live-action media.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:32.640 --> 00:11:38.400
The middle of the season focuses on Reyes' very&nbsp;
mystic storyline. By no coincidence, this season&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:38.400 --> 00:11:43.440
of "S.H.I.E.L.D." aired around the same time&nbsp;
2016's "Doctor Strange" was released in theaters.

00:11:43.920 --> 00:11:48.600
After Season 4 of "Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D."&nbsp;
introduces you to Robbie Reyes, aka the Spirit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:48.600 --> 00:11:53.820
of Vengeance, it's the perfect time to meet&nbsp;
Daimon and Satana "Ana" Helstrom. The series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:53.820 --> 00:11:58.080
"Helstrom," has a darker tone than some&nbsp;
of Marvel's other shows, and Daimon and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:58.080 --> 00:12:02.880
Ana definitely aren't your typical heroes. The&nbsp;
siblings, played by Tom Austen and Sydney Lemmon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:02.880 --> 00:12:07.980
are the offspring of a prolific serial killer.&nbsp;
On a quest to redeem their family legacy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:07.980 --> 00:12:11.820
they use their occult know-how to&nbsp;
hunt down the worst of humanity.

00:12:11.820 --> 00:12:14.220
Watching "Helstrom" after "S.H.I.E.L.D." Season 4&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:14.220 --> 00:12:19.380
is perfect timing from a thematic standpoint.&nbsp;
It's also the only true standalone series on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:19.380 --> 00:12:23.743
this list, as it doesn't cross over with&nbsp;
"S.H.I.E.L.D." or any other Marvel shows.

00:12:23.743 --> 00:12:27.840
On its surface, Freeform's "Cloak&nbsp;
&amp; Dagger" looks like a standalone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:27.840 --> 00:12:31.920
show. It's set in New Orleans rather than&nbsp;
New York, and it follows two superpowered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:31.920 --> 00:12:35.880
teens – Tyrone Johnson, played by&nbsp;
Aubrey Joseph, and Tandy Bowen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:35.880 --> 00:12:40.500
played by Olivia Holt — rather than adult&nbsp;
superheroes. However, comic book fans might&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:40.500 --> 00:12:44.940
notice "Cloak &amp; Dagger" has more connections&nbsp;
to the MCU than a passing glance indicates.

00:12:44.940 --> 00:12:48.540
The presence of the Roxxon Corp.&nbsp;
— a crooked energy corporation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:48.540 --> 00:12:53.340
and Cloak and Dagger's primary antagonist —&nbsp;
connects the series to the "Iron Man'' franchise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:53.340 --> 00:12:58.260
"Agent Carter," "Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D.," and&nbsp;
Marvel's former Netflix shows. In Season 1,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:58.260 --> 00:13:02.340
this program's dynamic duo's frenemy in&nbsp;
the police department Brigid O'Reilly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:02.340 --> 00:13:07.200
played by Emma Lahana, mentions knowing Misty&nbsp;
Knight, played by Simone Missick. Season 2&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:07.200 --> 00:13:11.280
includes a scene where Tyrone discusses&nbsp;
a newspaper article about Luke Cage.

00:13:11.280 --> 00:13:16.380
However, despite the show's indirect connections&nbsp;
to several of the aforementioned Marvel shows,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:16.380 --> 00:13:19.560
both seasons of "Cloak &amp; Dagger"&nbsp;
are perfectly placed here,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:19.560 --> 00:13:24.300
because the biggest crossover of the&nbsp;
series is with the next show on our list.

00:13:24.840 --> 00:13:25.800
"What do we do?”

00:13:25.800 --> 00:13:26.700
“We run."

00:13:26.700 --> 00:13:31.860
Despite Season 2's decline in ratings, "Cloak&nbsp;
&amp; Dagger" proved that an audience for teen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:31.860 --> 00:13:37.440
superheroes definitely exists, which can also&nbsp;
be said of Marvel's "Runaways." The show follows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:37.440 --> 00:13:41.940
six Los Angeles teens who unite against their&nbsp;
criminal parents, discovering their superpowers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:41.940 --> 00:13:47.220
in the process. As it happens, one of their powers&nbsp;
entails psychic communication with a dinosaur.

00:13:47.220 --> 00:13:52.080
"Runaways" premiered on Hulu in 2017,&nbsp;
and is set around the same general time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:52.080 --> 00:13:56.820
as "Cloak &amp; Dagger." Tandy and Tyrone even&nbsp;
appear in two episodes of "Runaways" Season 3.

00:13:56.820 --> 00:14:01.740
Along with its "Cloak &amp; Dagger '' crossover,&nbsp;
Season 3 of "Runaways' ' might also connect&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:01.740 --> 00:14:05.040
the show to the wider MCU by&nbsp;
introducing Morgan le Fey,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:05.040 --> 00:14:09.180
played by Elizabeth Hurley. The sinister&nbsp;
sorceress attempts to wield the power of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:09.180 --> 00:14:14.400
the Darkhold — a tome of dark magic last seen at&nbsp;
the end of Season 4 of "Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:14.400 --> 00:14:19.320
when Ghost Rider takes it to hell. Maybe we&nbsp;
shouldn't assume Morgan le Fey's Darkhold and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:19.320 --> 00:14:24.101
Ghost Rider's Darkhold are the same grimoire&nbsp;
... but we can't assume they aren't, either.

00:14:24.101 --> 00:14:28.920
For the most part, "Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D."&nbsp;
might as well exist on its own timeline during&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:28.920 --> 00:14:34.980
its final three seasons. However, a few brief&nbsp;
events from Season 5 tie in with 2017's "Thor:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:34.980 --> 00:14:40.440
Ragnarok" and 2018's "Avengers: Infinity&nbsp;
War," which makes the last three years of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:40.440 --> 00:14:45.240
"S.H.I.E.L.D." a perfect TV binge to&nbsp;
bring the MCU's Phase 3 to a close.

00:14:45.240 --> 00:14:50.520
The first half of "S.H.I.E.L.D." Season 5 is set&nbsp;
in a dystopian future which has no bearing on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:50.520 --> 00:14:55.800
MCU timeline. However, an off-the-cuff remark from&nbsp;
Noah, played by Joel David Moore, in Episode 11&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:55.800 --> 00:15:01.080
about an Asgardian walking the streets of New York&nbsp;
— presumably a reference to Thor's visit to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:01.080 --> 00:15:06.480
Big Apple in "Ragnarok" – gives Season 5 a loose&nbsp;
sense of place within the larger MCU timeline.

00:15:06.480 --> 00:15:10.200
However, even though the end of&nbsp;
Season 5 runs alongside "Avengers:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:10.200 --> 00:15:15.360
Infinity War," the season doesn't end with&nbsp;
the snap. According to showrunner Jed Whedon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:15.360 --> 00:15:19.380
the minds behind "S.H.I.E.L.D" avoided the&nbsp;
major plot point out of concern that their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:19.380 --> 00:15:23.940
unpredictable broadcast schedule could lead to&nbsp;
"S.H.I.E.L.D." accidentally spoiling the movie.

00:15:23.940 --> 00:15:28.800
The final season of "S.H.I.E.L.D." sees the&nbsp;
team literally jumping through time. During&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:28.800 --> 00:15:33.540
a "S.H.I.E.L.D." adventure in 1955, the show&nbsp;
resolves the question of Peggy Carter and Daniel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:33.540 --> 00:15:38.640
Sousa's relationship status ... which seems a&nbsp;
little redundant, considering 2019's "Avengers:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:38.640 --> 00:15:43.260
Endgame" makes it pretty clear she ends up&nbsp;
with Steve Rogers, played by Chris Evans.

00:15:43.680 --> 00:15:46.560
"It wasn't so hard to fit in, after all.”

00:15:46.560 --> 00:15:50.397
“And all we had to do was be ourselves.”

00:15:50.397 --> 00:15:52.634
“Well, with a few modifications."

00:15:52.680 --> 00:15:57.900
By the time the events of the MCU's designated&nbsp;
Phase 4 begins, Marvel Television has been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:57.900 --> 00:16:03.060
absorbed by Marvel Studios in the real&nbsp;
world. As a consequence, Marvel TV shows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:03.060 --> 00:16:08.520
greenlit after this point tend to sync up with&nbsp;
the films more overtly than we'd gotten used to.

00:16:08.520 --> 00:16:14.100
The 2021 limited series "WandaVision" is the&nbsp;
first show in an extensive line of Marvel series&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:14.100 --> 00:16:19.380
for the Disney+ streaming platform. Elizabeth&nbsp;
Olsen and Paul Bettany reprise their roles as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:19.380 --> 00:16:24.180
Wanda Maximoff and The Vision, and the story&nbsp;
spins off directly from "Avengers: Endgame."

00:16:24.180 --> 00:16:27.600
"WandaVision" has particularly&nbsp;
transformative implications for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:27.600 --> 00:16:31.620
Wanda. The tale ends with her officially&nbsp;
claiming the title of the Scarlet Witch,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:31.620 --> 00:16:37.740
after years of everyone acting like her superhero&nbsp;
codename was "Wanda". "WandaVision" also sets up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:37.740 --> 00:16:42.420
the Scarlet Witch's character arc for 2022's&nbsp;
"Doctor Strange in the Multiverse of Madness."

00:16:42.420 --> 00:16:48.600
While the series does a lot to move Marvel TV&nbsp;
forward, "WandaVision" also links back to past&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:48.600 --> 00:16:53.640
Marvel projects. Wanda gains possession of&nbsp;
a book called "the Darkhold" — which could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:53.640 --> 00:16:58.440
connect "WandaVision" to "Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D."&nbsp;
and "Runaways." But more directly, "WandaVision"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:58.440 --> 00:17:03.480
reintroduces characters from other MCU films,&nbsp;
including Darcy Lewis, played by Kat Dennings,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:03.480 --> 00:17:08.400
from the first two Thor movies, and Jimmy Woo,&nbsp;
played by Randall Park, from 2018's "Ant-Man&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:08.400 --> 00:17:13.620
and the Wasp." Hopefully, the speculation of&nbsp;
a Darcy and Woo spinoff proves to be accurate.

00:17:13.980 --> 00:17:18.000
After the events of "Avengers: Endgame,"&nbsp;
Sam Wilson, played by Anthony Mackie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:18.000 --> 00:17:22.620
and Bucky Barnes, played by Sebastian Stan,&nbsp;
reunite in "The Falcon and the Winter Soldier."

00:17:22.620 --> 00:17:27.780
In this single-season series, Sam and Bucky are&nbsp;
both dealing with their grief over Steve Rogers'&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:27.780 --> 00:17:32.520
departure from their lives in their own ways.&nbsp;
The story kicks off when Sam rejects Captain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:32.520 --> 00:17:37.020
America's shield, while Bucky faces up to the&nbsp;
acts of horrific violence he committed during&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:37.020 --> 00:17:40.620
his time as the Winter Soldier. "Falcon&nbsp;
and the Winter Soldier" dives into the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:40.620 --> 00:17:45.540
backstory of both central characters while&nbsp;
following its central plotline — multiple&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:45.540 --> 00:17:50.040
groups attempting to foil an anarchist&nbsp;
organization known as the Flag Smashers.

00:17:50.040 --> 00:17:54.180
"The Falcon and the Winter Soldier" serves&nbsp;
as a stepping-stone for these characters to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:54.180 --> 00:17:58.920
reach their next steps in the MCU. Eventually,&nbsp;
"Falcon and the Winter Soldier" concludes with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:58.920 --> 00:18:04.140
Sam taking on the mantle of Captain America&nbsp;
and, of course, receiving his new costume.

00:18:04.500 --> 00:18:08.700
Christmas of 2024, remember, the MCU&nbsp;
is a few years ahead of the real world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:08.700 --> 00:18:14.640
sees semi-retired Avenger Clint Barton, aka&nbsp;
Hawkeye, played by Jeremy Renner, back in action&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:14.640 --> 00:18:19.920
with an unofficial protégé, Kate Bishop, played by&nbsp;
Hailee Steinfeld. Kate prefers to think of herself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:19.920 --> 00:18:24.300
as Clint's partner rather than his sidekick,&nbsp;
but let's not waste time splitting hairs...

00:18:24.300 --> 00:18:28.620
The series takes place after "Avengers:&nbsp;
Endgame," "WandaVision," and "The Falcon and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:28.620 --> 00:18:33.300
the Winter Soldier." It also sets up at least&nbsp;
one upcoming Marvel show by introducing Echo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:33.300 --> 00:18:38.100
played by Alaqua Cox, and establishing&nbsp;
her connection with Wilson Fisk — played,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:38.100 --> 00:18:41.040
as he is in "Daredevil," by Vincent D'Onofrio.

00:18:41.040 --> 00:18:46.320
"Hawkeye" is billed as a limited series. A&nbsp;
second season hasn't been officially ruled out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:46.320 --> 00:18:51.180
but even if we never get more episodes of&nbsp;
"Hawkeye" it seems reasonable to expect more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:51.180 --> 00:18:56.760
from its characters, particularly Echo, Kate,&nbsp;
and Yelena Belova, played by Florence Pugh.

00:18:56.760 --> 00:19:02.447
"Kate Bishop! Hi!"

00:19:02.460 --> 00:19:06.960
The first season of "Loki" technically&nbsp;
takes place straight after "Avengers:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:06.960 --> 00:19:12.120
Endgame," around the same time as "WandaVision,"&nbsp;
although it was released between "The Falcon and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:12.120 --> 00:19:17.040
the Winter Soldier" and "Hawkeye." However, the&nbsp;
show's place in the chronological timeline gets&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:17.040 --> 00:19:23.220
a little funky, as "Loki" takes viewers back&nbsp;
to 2012, introduces a series of new timelines,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:23.220 --> 00:19:26.580
and eventually confirms the&nbsp;
existence of the Multiverse.

00:19:26.580 --> 00:19:31.500
The series ends with Tom Hiddleston's God&nbsp;
of Mischief fracturing the multiverse and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:31.500 --> 00:19:36.780
landing in an alternate reality where a&nbsp;
presumably evil variant of He Who Remains,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:36.780 --> 00:19:40.440
played by Jonathan Majors, rules&nbsp;
over The Time Variance Authority.

00:19:40.440 --> 00:19:44.940
"Loki'' adds an element of chaos and&nbsp;
creates infinite possibilities for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:44.940 --> 00:19:49.680
MCU. Like "WandaVision'' and "The Falcon and&nbsp;
the Winter Soldier," "Loki'' is an important&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:49.680 --> 00:19:53.640
part of the Marvel canon, shaping the&nbsp;
future of the multiverse saga. It's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:53.640 --> 00:19:59.334
also the only live-action Disney+ Marvel&nbsp;
show so far with a confirmed Season 2.

00:19:59.334 --> 00:20:01.740
"What If...?" fits nicely alongside

00:20:01.740 --> 00:20:06.060
"Loki," as its premiere ties into&nbsp;
the cliffhanger of "Loki" Season 1.

00:20:06.060 --> 00:20:10.620
The series sees characters like Captain&nbsp;
Carter and the Star Lord version of T'Challa&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:10.620 --> 00:20:14.820
make their MCU debut. "What If...?" also&nbsp;
welcomes Marvel film actors like Benedict&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:14.820 --> 00:20:18.000
Cumberbatch and Chris Hemsworth who&nbsp;
made their debut on the television&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:18.000 --> 00:20:22.560
side of things by voicing versions of their&nbsp;
big screen characters. Tragically, "What&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:22.560 --> 00:20:27.180
If..." includes one of the final performances&nbsp;
from "Black Panther" star Chadwick Boseman.

00:20:27.180 --> 00:20:30.000
After Captain Carter crossed&nbsp;
over into "Doctor Strange&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:32.820
in the Multiverse of Madness",&nbsp;
the possibility for more "What&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:32.820 --> 00:20:37.008
if…?" characters to cross over into&nbsp;
live action is very much a reality.

00:20:37.020 --> 00:20:41.640
Oscar Isaac makes his MCU debut&nbsp;
as Marc Spector and Stephen Grant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:41.640 --> 00:20:45.960
in "Moon Knight," the next installment&nbsp;
in Marvel's Phase 4 television roster,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:45.960 --> 00:20:52.320
and the first to reach the small screen in 2022.&nbsp;
The series definitely takes place after the Blip,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:52.320 --> 00:20:57.240
since an ad for the Global Repatriation&nbsp;
Council, or GRC, is visible in Episode 2.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:57.240 --> 00:21:01.980
As viewers might remember, the GRC makes its first&nbsp;
appearance in "The Falcon and the Winter Soldier."

00:21:01.980 --> 00:21:05.700
Release order is, of course, not the&nbsp;
only factor in the placement of "Moon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:05.700 --> 00:21:09.420
Knight" on this list. The series&nbsp;
establishes itself as more of a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:09.420 --> 00:21:13.500
standalone show that delves into Isaac's&nbsp;
character or, to put it more precisely,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:13.500 --> 00:21:17.879
his characters. Executive producer Grant&nbsp;
Curtis explained in a press release,

00:21:21.780 --> 00:21:27.000
However, that doesn't mean Isaac's appearance&nbsp;
is a one-off. In fact, it's quite the opposite,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:27.000 --> 00:21:31.080
as Marvel Studios President Kevin Feige&nbsp;
confirmed to The Hollywood Reporter that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:31.080 --> 00:21:35.328
Moon Knight will cross over with the&nbsp;
MCU films at some point in the future.

00:21:35.501 --> 00:21:43.181
"Good is not a thing you are,&nbsp;
Kamala, It's a thing you do."

00:21:43.260 --> 00:21:49.560
Next up on this list is "Ms. Marvel", the teen&nbsp;
superhero series starring Iman Vellani as Kamala&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:49.560 --> 00:21:54.600
Khan. Like Oscar Isaac's characters, Vellani&nbsp;
introduces the well-known comic book hero,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:54.600 --> 00:22:00.060
Ms. Marvel, to the screen. However, her character&nbsp;
is not an exact translation of the comics.

00:22:00.060 --> 00:22:03.600
While Vellani's character might&nbsp;
not be exactly the same on screen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:03.600 --> 00:22:07.920
she has been hailed for bringing wider&nbsp;
diversity to the superhero world. "Ms.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:07.920 --> 00:22:12.720
Marvel" follows Kamala as she uncovers and&nbsp;
comes into her superhero powers, and It's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:12.720 --> 00:22:18.300
not long before she discovers all the secrets and&nbsp;
dangers that come along with her mystic bangle.

00:22:18.300 --> 00:22:23.100
Marvel viewers who love "Hawkeye" will&nbsp;
adore this series, as both begin similarly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:23.100 --> 00:22:27.420
with Kate and Kamala fawning over their&nbsp;
favorite Avengers. However, unlike Kate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:27.420 --> 00:22:31.800
who faces the Tracksuit Mafia with Clint as&nbsp;
her partner, Kamala tries to figure out her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:31.800 --> 00:22:36.300
other-worldly powers on her own — or at least&nbsp;
with the help of Bruno, played by Matt Lintz,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:36.300 --> 00:22:41.160
and Kamran, played by Rish Shah. She doesn't&nbsp;
even get to meet her hero, though they do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:41.160 --> 00:22:46.920
seemingly swap places in the finale's post-credits&nbsp;
scene, which sets up an exciting Phase 4 team.

00:22:46.920 --> 00:22:50.880
Ms. Marvel will next appear alongside&nbsp;
Brie Larson's Captain Marvel and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:50.880 --> 00:22:54.960
Teyonah Parris's Monica Rambeau&nbsp;
in the 2023 film "The Marvels."

00:22:55.380 --> 00:23:01.440
Like Oscar Isaac and Iman Vellani, Tatiana Maslany&nbsp;
debuts a new MCU superhero on the small screen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:01.440 --> 00:23:07.200
taking on the role of lawyer Jennifer Walters, or&nbsp;
She-Hulk. Jennifer gets her powers after her blood&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:07.200 --> 00:23:11.700
becomes contaminated with her cousin Bruce&nbsp;
Banner's after a car accident. Mark Ruffalo&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:11.700 --> 00:23:16.740
reprises his role as Bruce and Smart Hulk to train&nbsp;
his cousin. However, it quickly becomes clear that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:16.740 --> 00:23:22.080
she's got a better handle on her abilities and&nbsp;
can learn in hours things that took him years.

00:23:22.080 --> 00:23:26.640
"She-Hulk" continues the development of new&nbsp;
Phase 4 characters also seen in "Hawkeye,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:26.640 --> 00:23:31.020
"Moon Knight," and "Ms. Marvel," but it also&nbsp;
links back to the wider MCU. With Jennifer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:31.020 --> 00:23:36.120
in her new role at Goodman Lieber Kurtzberg &amp;&nbsp;
Holliway, she practices law as her Hulk-self&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:36.120 --> 00:23:40.740
and works with a handful of superhuman&nbsp;
clients who MCU viewers have seen before.

00:23:40.740 --> 00:23:45.600
"She-Hulk" even picks up one of the unresolved&nbsp;
storylines from "Shang-Chi and the Legend of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:45.600 --> 00:23:50.580
the Ten Rings," explaining what happened after&nbsp;
Wong, played by Benedict Wong, and Emil Blonsky,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:50.580 --> 00:23:56.100
aka Abomination, played by Tim Roth, fought in&nbsp;
Xialing's club. As the series reaches its climax,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:56.100 --> 00:24:01.260
vigilante hero Daredevil, played by Charlie Cox,&nbsp;
joins the flight, helping the good guys win,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:01.260 --> 00:24:05.580
and the ending leaves for Jen and&nbsp;
Bruce to appear again in the MCU.

